# How we work

You prompt and decide product behavior. The agent writes code. Each of you QAs on your own identity.

| Fixture | Who |
|---|---|
| `.local/test-pn/` | You, on your machine |

The agent never opens, unlocks, or uploads `.local/test-pn/`. Fixture boundaries: `local-test-pn.mdc`. Verification (tests, no browser MCP by default): `agent-scope.mdc`. Hard bans: `auth-trust-boundary.mdc`.

## Precedence

When this chat and a rule or doc disagree, follow the chat. Do not implement a path the chat just rejected. Do not mark the requested behavior as follow-on or out of scope because a spec says so.

## Root cause before the first edit

Name the user-visible symptom, the path from that action to the external system (Drive, API, Redis, Postgres, or the device), and the function on that path that returns early, returns null, or swallows the error. The edit goes on that path. A UI change that hides the symptom while that boundary still fails is not the fix. If that path cannot be read, stop and say so. Do not guess a patch.

## Architecture

Once that path is identified: one implementation in `packages/` (apps stay thin). Delete the wrong dual, shim, or second resolver. Leave a path that is already correct alone. Do not rebuild a subsystem as a substitute for the trace. Do not leave the broken path beside the fix.

## Workflow tests in the same change

A new user-facing workflow in any app or package lands with a test file next to the code. The test calls the workflow and asserts the outcome. It uses that package's existing runner (Vitest or Jest) and that package's existing test script. If that package is missing from root `package.json` `"test"`, add one `test:<app>` entry to that root script in the same change. Dashboard and browse are already on it. Pen and Prism have test scripts and are not.

## Done

Hermetic tests pass for the touched area; crypto and auth stay on package tests. Report what was run and what was not verified (e.g. live API, UI). Files written and todos checked are not done alone. Your confirmation on your own pN is what makes visible flows onboarding-ready. See `agent-scope.mdc`.

## Hard-ban ratchets

`scripts/check-*.sh` is only for a new hard ban. Do not weaken, skip, or grow allowlists. A workflow test is a package test file, not a new check script.
